<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.130 percent from 10.140 percent at the previous auction on December 5.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: March 13, 1997 (March 6, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.130 percent (10.140)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 841.800 million (868.500 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 908.050 million (1.005 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.150 percent (10.002-10.158)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.209 percent (10.002-10.538)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 125 (129)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 131 (155)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
